<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>Power Platform Monitoring Framework — Release Notes</title>
  <style>
    :root {
      --primary:          #0078d4;
      --primary-dark:     #005a9e;
      --primary-light:    #e1effa;
      --success:          #107c10;
      --success-light:    #f0faf0;
      --success-border:   #c3e6c3;
      --warning-light:    #fffbee;
      --warning-border:   #fde7a0;
      --error:            #d13438;
      --error-light:      #fff3f3;
      --error-border:     #f3c6c7;
      --bg:               #f3f2f1;
      --surface:          #ffffff;
      --border:           #edebe9;
      --border-strong:    #8a8886;
      --text:             #323130;
      --text-secondary:   #605e5c;
      --text-disabled:    #a19f9d;
      --radius:           4px;
      --shadow:           0 1.6px 3.6px rgba(0,0,0,.13), 0 .3px .9px rgba(0,0,0,.11);
    }

    *, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }

    body {
      font-family: 'Segoe UI', system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;
      font-size: 14px;
      line-height: 1.6;
      color: var(--text);
      background: var(--bg);
      min-height: 100vh;
    }

    /* ── Header ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    .app-header {
      background: var(--primary);
      color: #fff;
      padding: 18px 32px;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 16px;
    }
    .app-header-icon {
      width: 40px; height: 40px;
      background: rgba(255,255,255,.18);
      border-radius: var(--radius);
      display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
      font-size: 22px;
      flex-shrink: 0;
    }
    .app-header h1 { font-size: 18px; font-weight: 600; }
    .app-header p  { font-size: 12px; opacity: .85; margin-top: 2px; }

    /* ── Layout ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    .app-body { display: flex; min-height: calc(100vh - 76px); }

    .sidebar {
      width: 200px;
      flex-shrink: 0;
      background: var(--surface);
      border-right: 1px solid var(--border);
      padding: 20px 0;
      position: sticky;
      top: 0;
      height: calc(100vh - 76px);
      overflow-y: auto;
    }

    .sidebar-section-label {
      font-size: 10px;
      font-weight: 700;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: .08em;
      color: var(--text-disabled);
      padding: 12px 20px 4px;
    }
    .sidebar-section-label:first-child { padding-top: 4px; }

    .sidebar a {
      display: block;
      padding: 7px 20px;
      font-size: 13px;
      color: var(--text-secondary);
      text-decoration: none;
      border-left: 3px solid transparent;
      transition: color .1s, background .1s, border-color .1s;
    }
    .sidebar a:hover { color: var(--primary); background: var(--primary-light); }
    .sidebar a.active { color: var(--primary); border-left-color: var(--primary); background: var(--primary-light); font-weight: 600; }

    .app-main { flex: 1; padding: 28px 36px; max-width: 860px; overflow-y: auto; }

    /* ── Release card ────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    .release-card {
      background: var(--surface);
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: var(--radius);
      box-shadow: var(--shadow);
      margin-bottom: 28px;
      scroll-margin-top: 20px;
    }
    .release-header {
      padding: 16px 20px;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 12px;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
    }
    .release-version {
      font-size: 16px;
      font-weight: 700;
      color: var(--text);
      font-family: 'Cascadia Code', 'Consolas', monospace;
    }
    .release-date {
      font-size: 12px;
      color: var(--text-disabled);
      margin-left: auto;
    }
    .release-body { padding: 20px; }

    /* ── Change type badges ──────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    .badge {
      display: inline-block; padding: 2px 8px;
      border-radius: 10px; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 600;
    }
    .badge-new      { background: #dce9f8; color: #004578; }
    .badge-improved { background: var(--success-border); color: #0e5a0e; }
    .badge-fixed    { background: var(--error-border); color: #6b0c0e; }
    .badge-changed  { background: var(--warning-border); color: #4d3700; }

    /* ── Change list ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    .change-group { margin-bottom: 18px; }
    .change-group:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
    .change-group-title {
      font-size: 11px;
      font-weight: 700;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: .06em;
      color: var(--text-disabled);
      margin-bottom: 8px;
      padding-bottom: 4px;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    }
    .change-list {
      list-style: none;
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 6px;
    }
    .change-item {
      display: flex;
      gap: 10px;
      align-items: flex-start;
      font-size: 13px;
    }
    .change-item .badge { flex-shrink: 0; margin-top: 1px; }
    .change-item-text { color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.5; }
    .change-item-text strong { color: var(--text); }

    code {
      font-family: 'Cascadia Code', 'Consolas', monospace;
      font-size: 12px;
      background: var(--bg);
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 3px;
      padding: 1px 5px;
      color: var(--primary-dark);
    }

    /* ── Buttons ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    .btn {
      display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 5px;
      height: 32px; padding: 0 16px;
      border: none; border-radius: var(--radius);
      font-family: inherit; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600;
      cursor: pointer;
      text-decoration: none;
    }
    .btn-secondary { background: transparent; color: #fff; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.5); }
    .btn-secondary:hover { background: rgba(255,255,255,.12); }
    .btn-sm { height: 26px; padding: 0 10px; font-size: 12px; }

    /* ── Responsive ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    @media (max-width: 740px) {
      .sidebar { display: none; }
      .app-main { padding: 16px; }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     Header
════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div class="app-header">
  <div class="app-header-icon">📋</div>
  <div>
    <h1>Power Platform Monitoring Framework</h1>
    <p>Release Notes</p>
  </div>
  <div style="margin-left:auto">
    <a class="btn btn-secondary btn-sm" href="ppmf_docs" target="_blank">📖 Documentation</a>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="app-body">

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       Sidebar Navigation
  ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <nav class="sidebar" id="sidebar">
    <div class="sidebar-section-label">Releases</div>
    <a href="#v1-0-0-11" class="active">v1.0.0.11</a>
    <a href="#v1-0-0-10">v1.0.0.10</a>
    <a href="#v1-0-0-9">v1.0.0.9</a>
    <a href="#v1-0-0-8">v1.0.0.8</a>
  </nav>

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       Main Content
  ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <main class="app-main" id="main-content">

    <!-- ── v1.0.0.11 ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <div class="release-card" id="v1-0-0-11">
      <div class="release-header">
        <span class="release-version">v1.0.0.11</span>
        <span class="badge badge-new" style="font-size:12px">Latest</span>
        <span class="release-date">May 8, 2026</span>
      </div>
      <div class="release-body">

        <div class="change-group">
          <div class="change-group-title">Configuration — Connection Reference Review</div>
          <ul class="change-list">
            <li class="change-item">
              <span class="badge badge-new">New</span>
              <span class="change-item-text"><strong>Connection Reference Review page</strong> — new page under Configuration in the PPMF Platform Monitor app. Displays assignment status, record owner, solution membership, and dependent flow count for every connection reference in the environment. Unassigned references are highlighted with a callout. Includes a filter bar (search, status, connector, solution, owner, hide system references) and expandable rows showing dependent flows with active/inactive state pills.</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="change-group">
          <div class="change-group-title">ALM — Deployment Tooling</div>
          <ul class="change-list">
            <li class="change-item">
              <span class="badge badge-new">New</span>
              <span class="change-item-text"><strong>Post-deploy health check script</strong> (<code>scripts/Test-PPMFDeployment.ps1</code>) — validates a PPMF deployment is complete and correctly configured. Checks solution version, all 11 flows, all 3 connection references, all 12 environment variable definitions, all 4 security roles, and key web resources. Runs automatically in the CI/CD pipeline after every import.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="change-item">
              <span class="badge badge-new">New</span>
              <span class="change-item-text"><strong>Dev CI/CD pipeline</strong> (<code>deploy-dev.yml</code>) — GitHub Actions workflow that packs and imports the solution to the dev environment on push to <code>dev</code>, then runs the health check to validate the deployment.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="change-item">
              <span class="badge badge-new">New</span>
              <span class="change-item-text"><strong>Release pipeline</strong> (<code>release.yml</code>) — GitHub Actions workflow triggered on version tag push. Packs managed and unmanaged zips, publishes a GitHub Release with changelog content, imports to production, re-activates flows, runs the health check, and syncs <code>main</code> back into <code>dev</code> automatically.</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ── v1.0.0.10 ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <div class="release-card" id="v1-0-0-10">
      <div class="release-header">
        <span class="release-version">v1.0.0.10</span>
        <span class="release-date">May 4, 2026</span>
      </div>
      <div class="release-body">

        <div class="change-group">
          <div class="change-group-title">Portability — SharePoint Error Store</div>
          <ul class="change-list">
            <li class="change-item">
              <span class="badge badge-new">New</span>
              <span class="change-item-text"><strong>Writing Mode environment variable</strong> (<code>ppmf_WritingMode</code>) — controls where error events are written. <strong>Dataverse</strong> (default, existing behavior), <strong>SharePoint</strong> (no Dataverse required), or <strong>Both</strong> (dual-store). Zero change to existing Dataverse deployments — default is <code>Dataverse</code>.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="change-item">
              <span class="badge badge-new">New</span>
              <span class="change-item-text"><strong>PPMF-Child-WriteErrorToSharePoint</strong> — sibling to <code>PPMF-Child-FlowWritetoIntakeList</code>. Accepts the same <code>ErrorPayload</code> JSON contract. Performs a deduplication check against the SharePoint list <code>FlowRunId</code> column before creating a list item. Responds with the same <code>result</code>/<code>recordid</code> schema for caller compatibility.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="change-item">
              <span class="badge badge-new">New</span>
              <span class="change-item-text"><strong>PPMF-Child-FlowErrorHandler-SharePoint</strong> — full error handler for SharePoint mode. Replicates the error classification and severity logic from <code>PPMF-Child-FlowErrorHandler-JSON</code>. Calls <code>PPMF-Child-WriteErrorToSharePoint</code>, then conditionally posts a Teams alert card. Accepts a <code>SuppressTeamsAlert</code> input parameter so the <strong>Both</strong> mode caller can suppress the duplicate card from the SharePoint leg.</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="change-group">
          <div class="change-group-title">SharePoint → Dataverse Sync Flow</div>
          <ul class="change-list">
            <li class="change-item">
              <span class="badge badge-new">New</span>
              <span class="change-item-text"><strong>PPMF-Sync-SharePointErrorsToDataverse</strong> — recurrence flow (every 15 minutes) that promotes unsynced SharePoint error items into the Dataverse <code>ppmf_errorevent</code> table. Ships in the <strong>Off</strong> state; must be turned on manually when Dataverse is available. Deduplicates against <code>ppmf_flowrunid</code> before inserting. Uses a dead-letter cap of 3 failed sync attempts per item to prevent queue stall. Updates <code>SyncedToDataverse</code>, <code>DataverseRecordId</code>, <code>SyncAttempts</code>, and <code>LastSyncAttempt</code> columns on each SharePoint item.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="change-item">
              <span class="badge badge-new">New</span>
              <span class="change-item-text"><strong>Dataverse Sync Enabled variable</strong> (<code>ppmf_DataverseSyncEnabled</code>) — soft enable/disable for the sync flow. Defaults to <code>No</code>. When <code>No</code>, the recurrence trigger fires but the flow terminates immediately without processing any records. Allows the flow to remain scheduled while acting as a no-op until Dataverse is ready.</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="change-group">
          <div class="change-group-title">New Environment Variables</div>
          <ul class="change-list">
            <li class="change-item">
              <span class="badge badge-new">New</span>
              <span class="change-item-text"><strong>ppmf_WritingMode</strong> — write destination control. Values: <code>Dataverse</code> (default), <code>SharePoint</code>, <code>Both</code>.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="change-item">
              <span class="badge badge-new">New</span>
              <span class="change-item-text"><strong>ppmf_SharePointSiteUrl</strong> — full URL of the SharePoint site hosting the error events list. Required when Writing Mode is <code>SharePoint</code> or <code>Both</code>.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="change-item">
              <span class="badge badge-new">New</span>
              <span class="change-item-text"><strong>ppmf_SharePointListName</strong> — exact display name of the SharePoint list. Default: <code>PPMF Error Events</code>.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="change-item">
              <span class="badge badge-new">New</span>
              <span class="change-item-text"><strong>ppmf_DataverseSyncEnabled</strong> — soft enable for the sync flow. Default: <code>No</code>.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="change-item">
              <span class="badge badge-new">New</span>
              <span class="change-item-text"><strong>ppmf_SyncIntervalMinutes</strong> — documented recurrence interval. Default: <code>15</code>.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="change-item">
              <span class="badge badge-new">New</span>
              <span class="change-item-text"><strong>ppmf_SyncBatchSize</strong> — maximum items processed per sync run. Default: <code>100</code>.</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="change-group">
          <div class="change-group-title">Connection References</div>
          <ul class="change-list">
            <li class="change-item">
              <span class="badge badge-new">New</span>
              <span class="change-item-text"><strong>ppmf_SharePointConnectionReference</strong> — SharePoint Online connection reference. Required when Writing Mode is <code>SharePoint</code> or <code>Both</code>. Assign to an account with Contribute access to the target SharePoint site.</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="change-group">
          <div class="change-group-title">Flow Changes</div>
          <ul class="change-list">
            <li class="change-item">
              <span class="badge badge-changed">Changed</span>
              <span class="change-item-text"><strong>PPMF-Child-ProcessFlowError</strong> — added <code>ppmf_WritingMode</code> parameter binding. The <code>Scope-Record_Error</code> action is replaced by a <code>Switch_WritingMode</code> action that branches to the Dataverse handler (default), the SharePoint handler, or both in parallel based on the configured mode. No change to behavior when Writing Mode is <code>Dataverse</code>.</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="change-group">
          <div class="change-group-title">Setup &amp; Configuration Page</div>
          <ul class="change-list">
            <li class="change-item">
              <span class="badge badge-new">New</span>
              <span class="change-item-text"><strong>SharePoint Error Store card</strong> — new configuration section with Writing Mode selector (preset buttons for Dataverse / SharePoint / Both), SharePoint Site URL, SharePoint List Name, and Dataverse Sync Enabled fields. Section is always visible to prompt intentional configuration of Writing Mode.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="change-item">
              <span class="badge badge-new">New</span>
              <span class="change-item-text"><strong>Writing Mode check</strong> (<code>chk-writing-mode</code>) — validates that <code>ppmf_WritingMode</code> is set to a recognised value.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="change-item">
              <span class="badge badge-new">New</span>
              <span class="change-item-text"><strong>SharePoint configuration check</strong> (<code>chk-sp-config</code>) — validates SharePoint Site URL is set and the SharePoint connection reference is assigned when Writing Mode is <code>SharePoint</code> or <code>Both</code>. Shows pass with “Not applicable” when Writing Mode is <code>Dataverse</code>.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="change-item">
              <span class="badge badge-new">New</span>
              <span class="change-item-text"><strong>Sync flow state check</strong> (<code>chk-sync-flow</code>) — cross-validates the on/off state of <code>PPMF-Sync-SharePointErrorsToDataverse</code> against the <code>ppmf_DataverseSyncEnabled</code> variable. Warns if the flow is On but the variable is not <code>Yes</code>, or fails if the variable is <code>Yes</code> but the flow is Off.</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ── v1.0.0.9 ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <div class="release-card" id="v1-0-0-9">
      <div class="release-header">
        <span class="release-version">v1.0.0.9</span>
        <span class="release-date">May 3, 2026</span>
      </div>
      <div class="release-body">

        <div class="change-group">
          <div class="change-group-title">Forms</div>
          <ul class="change-list">
            <li class="change-item">
              <span class="badge badge-new">New</span>
              <span class="change-item-text"><strong>Error Event form section visibility</strong> — the Flow section and User section on the Error Event main form now show and hide automatically based on <code>ppmf_sourcetype</code>. Flow/Child Flow errors show the Flow section; Power App errors show the User section; unset records show both.</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="change-group">
          <div class="change-group-title">Web Resources</div>
          <ul class="change-list">
            <li class="change-item">
              <span class="badge badge-new">New</span>
              <span class="change-item-text"><strong>ppmf_base</strong> — foundation script establishing the shared <code>PPMF</code> namespace and <code>PPMF.utils</code> helper module (<code>setSectionVisible</code>, <code>getOptionSetValue</code>). Must be registered as the first library on any form using other PPMF scripts.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="change-item">
              <span class="badge badge-new">New</span>
              <span class="change-item-text"><strong>ppmf_errorEventForm</strong> — Error Event main form controller. Implements <code>PPMF.ErrorEvent.onLoad</code> and <code>PPMF.ErrorEvent.onSourceTypeChange</code> to apply section visibility rules on load and on change.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="change-item">
              <span class="badge badge-new">New</span>
              <span class="change-item-text"><strong>ppmf_releasenotes</strong> — this release notes page, accessible from the Documentation sidebar.</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="change-group">
          <div class="change-group-title">Documentation</div>
          <ul class="change-list">
            <li class="change-item">
              <span class="badge badge-improved">Improved</span>
              <span class="change-item-text"><strong>Error Event Field Glossary expanded</strong> — all 30+ custom fields now documented and organized into logical groups: Identity &amp; Intake, Capture Context, Error Detail, Canvas App, Triage, and Resolution Tracking.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="change-item">
              <span class="badge badge-fixed">Fixed</span>
              <span class="change-item-text"><strong>Incorrect schema names corrected</strong> — <code>ppmf_triagingstatus</code> corrected to <code>ppmf_triagestatus</code>; <code>ppmf_alertsent</code> (boolean) corrected to <code>ppmf_alertsenton</code> (datetime).</span>
            </li>
            <li class="change-item">
              <span class="badge badge-new">New</span>
              <span class="change-item-text"><strong>ppmf_sourcetype</strong> added to the Field Glossary with description of its form visibility behavior.</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ── v1.0.0.8 ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <div class="release-card" id="v1-0-0-8">
      <div class="release-header">
        <span class="release-version">v1.0.0.8</span>
        <span class="release-date">May 2026</span>
      </div>
      <div class="release-body">

        <div class="change-group">
          <div class="change-group-title">Initial Release</div>
          <ul class="change-list">
            <li class="change-item">
              <span class="badge badge-new">New</span>
              <span class="change-item-text"><strong>Core flow error capture</strong> — <code>PPMF-Child-ProcessFlowError</code> entry point parses <code>workflow()</code> JSON, extracts flow name and run ID, and constructs portal deep links.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="change-item">
              <span class="badge badge-new">New</span>
              <span class="change-item-text"><strong>Teams alerting</strong> — <code>PPMF-Child-FlowErrorHandler-JSON</code> and <code>PPMF-Child-FlowErrorHandler-Parameters</code> resolve alert routes, check throttle windows, and post adaptive card alerts to Teams.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="change-item">
              <span class="badge badge-new">New</span>
              <span class="change-item-text"><strong>Dataverse error logging</strong> — <code>PPMF-Child-FlowWritetoIntakeList</code> creates <code>ppmf_errorevent</code> records on every failure, regardless of throttle state.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="change-item">
              <span class="badge badge-new">New</span>
              <span class="change-item-text"><strong>Canvas App error handling</strong> — <code>PPMF-Power-Apps-Error-Handler-JSON</code> accepts a JSON error payload via PowerAppV2 trigger, applies throttle logic, and logs to Dataverse.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="change-item">
              <span class="badge badge-new">New</span>
              <span class="change-item-text"><strong>Alert Routes</strong> — <code>ppmf_alertroute</code> table enables per-solution Teams channel routing with configurable minimum severity thresholds.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="change-item">
              <span class="badge badge-new">New</span>
              <span class="change-item-text"><strong>Severity Badge</strong> — <code>ppmf_severityBadgeForm</code> renders a colored left-border indicator on the <code>ppmf_severity</code> header field on the Error Event form.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="change-item">
              <span class="badge badge-new">New</span>
              <span class="change-item-text"><strong>Automated retention</strong> — <code>PPMF-Delete-Old-Errors</code> runs weekly to delete resolved error records older than the configured retention threshold.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="change-item">
              <span class="badge badge-new">New</span>
              <span class="change-item-text"><strong>Setup &amp; Configuration page</strong> — guided post-import checklist with 8 automated deployment validation checks.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="change-item">
              <span class="badge badge-new">New</span>
              <span class="change-item-text"><strong>Documentation page</strong> — in-app HTML documentation covering architecture, configuration, field glossaries, and integration guides.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="change-item">
              <span class="badge badge-new">New</span>
              <span class="change-item-text"><strong>Demo flow</strong> — <code>PPMF-Demo-Flow-Failure</code> for end-to-end validation after setup.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="change-item">
              <span class="badge badge-new">New</span>
              <span class="change-item-text"><strong>Environment variables</strong> — six configurable variables: Environment Name, Portal Base URL, Teams Group ID, Flow Alerts Channel ID, Alert Throttle Minutes (default 15), and Error Retention Days (default 90).</span>
            </li>
            <li class="change-item">
              <span class="badge badge-new">New</span>
              <span class="change-item-text"><strong>Security roles</strong> — four roles included: PPMF Admin, PPMF Reader, PPMF Service Account, and PPMF Triager.</span>
